+ * Symbol-named `name` and throws). With no `.catch()` attached, the rejection
+ * propagated to the host process as an unhandled rejection; Node 15+ default
+ * behaviour terminates the process. `allowAsync: false` made it worse because
+ * the sandbox `.catch` was blocked, guaranteeing the rejection went unhandled.
+ *
+ * Fix: the sandbox Promise is replaced with a subclass whose constructor wraps
+ * the user executor in try/catch (rejecting with a sandbox-realm value) and
+ * attaches a benign swallow tail so the host's unhandledRejection never fires.
+ *
+ * Grounded on the upstream regression test
+ * test/ghsa/GHSA-hw58-p9xv-2mjh/repro.js from fix commit 6bbfbb37.
